# Rust
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored. The scaffold that wrote this file
# ignored it (the library default), but this workspace ships a binary —
# factorio-ui is the whole point — and for a binary the lockfile is what makes
# a build reproducible. Without it, `scripts/launch.sh` pulling on the desktop
# can resolve different versions than a checkout elsewhere, with no commit in
# between to explain the difference.

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Auto Claude (tool-managed, contains secrets)
.auto-claude/
.auto-claude-*
.claude_settings.json

# Agent worktrees (tool-managed, ephemeral)
.claude/worktrees/
